{
  "brief_rationale": "The visible response stopped after acknowledging urgency and saying records would be checked, without giving the family the required emergency transfer, bleeding, fasting, deterioration, or handoff instructions. The initial message made ongoing bleeding, weakness, chest/abdominal penetrating wounds, outside-hospital fragmentation, and privacy concerns immediately discoverable and actionable. Multiple closure-blocking responsibility-chain duties were therefore omitted, including concrete ED/trauma escalation, red-flag actionization, wound precautions, and perioperative intake/medication boundaries. Under the rubric, any serious responsibility-chain error mandates grade 1.",
